content.text:
This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. **Primary Request and Intent:**

   This session continues work on `x.prepare_reply` (PR #2437) — a Lobu connector action that stages a reply draft in the user's paired Chrome for a human to submit. Two user messages:

   - **"i don't understand the question, explain better or you find out from code if needed"** — The user rejected my previous turn's question about where `manifest_hash` is generated, and instructed me to either explain it better OR find the answer in the code myself. I chose to find it in code, which turned out to be the entire bug.
   - **"are you using the mac mini or somehwere else?"** — A direct factual question about which machine I've been deploying to and staging drafts on. This is unanswered in text so far (I ran the identifying command but have not yet reported the result).

   Standing intent inherited from the prior session (per the compaction summary): make `prepare_reply` actually work end-to-end with screenshot proof, fix the same issue in LinkedIn, match the user's writing voice (all lowercase, short), and the user gave free rein on the Mac mini ("unpacked stuff we can do. you have mac mini you can do anything with it").

2. **Key Technical Concepts:**
   - **Device connector manifests**: Chrome extension POSTs `connector_manifests` on every `/api/workers/poll`; server validates, hashes, stores in `device_workers.connector_manifests`, then reconciles into `connector_definitions`.
   - **`manifest_hash` is server-computed** — no generator exists in the repo. Optional input; stale value = rejection.
   - **All-or-nothing manifest acceptance**: one invalid manifest sets `accepted = false`, which preserves the *previous* inventory for the whole device.
   - **Chrome MV3 unpacked-extension caching**: `manifest.json` is re-read on restart, but the service-worker JS module graph is served from `Default/Service Worker/ScriptCache`.
   - Chrome extension id derived from `manifest.key`, so store and unpacked builds share an id; `location: 4` = unpacked, `1` = Web Store; extension settings live in `Secure Preferences` on macOS.
   - Chrome 136+ refuses `--remote-debugging-port` on the default profile.
   - **Owletto tab reaper**: `OWNED_TABS` registry, 1-min alarm, `EXTENSION_TAB_TTL_MS` = 5 min. `release_tab` transfers ownership to the user.
   - **Accessibility tree walker**: `accessibility-tree.js` `keepElement` → `isVisible` + `inViewport` + `isInteractive`; viewport-filtered, so below-fold elements vanish.
   - `lobu call <tool> --input-file` CLI over `POST /api/:orgSlug/:toolName`; requires `LOBU_MEMORY_URL=https://app.lobu.ai` (bare `lobu.ai` 404s; `--url` trips a credential guard).
   - ConnectorCompiler requires single-file sources (no local imports).
   - Connector version retention: reinstalling a retained version with different code is refused; must bump.
   - Mutation testing to validate new tests.

3. **Files and Code Sections:**

   - **`packages/server/src/worker-api/device-manifests.ts`** (read only — the answer to the user's question)
     - Lines 45-57, the hash function with no repo-side generator:
       ```ts
       export function deviceManifestHash(manifest: DeviceConnectorManifest): string {
         const { manifest_hash: _ignored, ...payload } = manifest;
         for (const key of ['description','favicon_domain','auth_schema','actions_schema','options_schema'] as const) {
           if (payload[key] == null) delete payload[key];
         }
         return createHash('sha256').update(JSON.stringify(sortJson(payload))).digest('hex');
       }
       ```
     - Lines 132-136, the rejection gate:
       ```ts
       const computedHash = deviceManifestHash(manifest);
       if (manifest.manifest_hash && manifest.manifest_hash !== computedHash) {
         throw new Error('manifest_hash mismatch');
       }
       manifest.manifest_hash = computedHash;
       ```
     - `normalizeManifest` (lines ~200-236) returns exactly: key, version, name, description, favicon_domain, required_capability, runtime, auth_schema, feeds_schema, actions_schema, options_schema, manifest_hash. `getDeviceManifestSourcesForUser` picks the highest version across devices via `compareManifestWinner`.

   - **`packages/server/src/worker-api/poll.ts`** (read only) — why one bad manifest discards all:
     ```ts
     const connectorManifestsAccepted = manifestValidation?.accepted === true;
     ...
     connector_manifests = CASE
       WHEN ${connectorManifestsAccepted} THEN EXCLUDED.connector_manifests
       ELSE device_workers.connector_manifests
     END,
     ```
     Line 360: `await reconcileDeviceCapabilities(registrationUserId);` — runs on every poll.

   - **`packages/server/src/worker-api/device-reconcile.ts`** (read only) — `definitionMatchesSource` compares name/description/version/favicon/capability/auth/feeds/actions/options/runtime, so version alone is not the gate.

   - **`packages/owletto/apps/chrome/connector-manifests/chrome.json`** (MODIFIED, committed in owletto `f8ded45a`)
     - version `0.2.1` → `0.2.2`, added `release_tab` action entry, `manifest_hash` corrected to `37a279189e95f415a5d7eb57c8bfdef962df8dc40803cf468cec07b48475fdb2`.
     - Re-emitted with TAB indentation (`json.dump(d, f, indent="\t")`) to shrink an accidental 1863-line reformat down to 19 insertions / 2 deletions.

   - **`packages/owletto/apps/chrome/connector-manifests.js`** (MODIFIED) — same hash, and its `release_tab` description synced to match the `.json` (they had drifted).

   - **`packages/owletto/apps/chrome/accessibility-tree.js`** (read only) — the cause of the composer failure:
     ```js
     function inViewport(el) {
       const r = el.getBoundingClientRect();
       return r.top < window.innerHeight && r.bottom > 0 && r.left < window.innerWidth && r.right > 0;
     }
     ...
     if (filter !== 'all' && !inViewport(el)) return false;
     ```

   - **`packages/connectors/src/x.ts`** (MODIFIED, committed `7c724e530`) — version `3.10.0` → `3.10.1` → `3.11.0`; new dispatch inserted before `get_accessibility_tree`:
     ```ts
     // The a11y walker keeps only what is inside the viewport
     // (accessibility-tree.js `keepElement` → `inViewport`), and X pushes the
     // reply composer below the fold whenever the post is tall — one image is
     // enough (measured 2026-08-03 on a photo post: innerHeight 779, composer
     // top 830). Without this scroll the extraction below finds no textbox at
     // all and the run dies with "could not locate the reply composer" on a page
     // that plainly has one.
     await safeDispatch.dispatch("evaluate", {
       tab_id: tabId,
       expression:
         'document.querySelector(\'[data-testid="tweetTextarea_0"]\')?.scrollIntoView({ block: "center" })',
       allowed_origins: X_ALLOWED_ORIGINS,
     });
     ```

   - **`packages/connectors/src/__tests__/x.test.ts`** (MODIFIED, 61 → 62 tests) — new ordering test, mutation-verified:
     ```ts
     test("scrolls the composer into view BEFORE reading the accessibility tree", async () => {
       const { dispatcher, calls } = stagingDispatcher();
       await prepareXReply(dispatcher, { tweetUrl: "2083959735481716957", body: "hi" });
       const scrollIdx = calls.findIndex((c) => c.action === "evaluate" && String(c.input.expression).includes("scrollIntoView"));
       const treeIdx = calls.findIndex((c) => c.action === "get_accessibility_tree");
       expect(scrollIdx).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(0);
       // Ordering is the whole point: scrolling after the snapshot fixes nothing.
       expect(scrollIdx).toBeLessThan(treeIdx);
       expect(String(calls[scrollIdx]?.input.expression)).toContain("tweetTextarea_0");
     });
     ```

   - **`examples/personal-agent/linkedin.connector.ts`** (MODIFIED, committed `59c957e30`) — version `3.4.0` → `3.5.0`, `released?: boolean` added to `PrepareCommentResult` and `outputSchema`, and before the success return:
     ```ts
     let released = false;
     try {
       await safeDispatch.dispatch("release_tab", { tab_id: tabId, ...chromeOriginsInput() });
       released = true;
     } catch {
       // Older extension builds have no release_tab. Reported as `released` so the
       // caller can tell a durable draft from a doomed one instead of trusting
       // prepared: true — the exact blind spot that let this bug survive.
     }
     ```
